Build 033 (from the 032 run: no freeze, crash "game memory exhausted" at 816 s after the autosave):
- The stall watchdog acts only when the GPU owes work (a channel pending, or syncpoint 1's guest
  value ahead of the host's); idle waits are counted (idle_waits) and not logged or recovered. In
  032 all 11 reports were an idle GPU while the guest loaded or saved.
- Memory probe: a fall of 192 MiB or more in the pool's largest free block against the reading of
  up to 1 s before (64 MiB under 768 MiB) logs EDEN_MEMORY_DROP and runs the texture cache's memory
  report at once (images, largest, formats, VMA types, dedicated images, staging pools), at most
  twice a second. EDEN_NX2_MEMORY_DROP_OFF / memory-drop-off.txt: off. Diagnostic only.
- Not changed: the caches' "memory in use" (graphics_usage.h already measures the shared pool; the
  6144 MiB seen in 032 was that formula at a nearly full pool, not a wrong figure).

